cabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le01ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking Someone to Slow Down"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you ask someone to speak slowly, it is important to be polite."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here are some phrases you can use to ask someone to speak slowing."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Slow down, please! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Speak slowly please, Miss/Sir. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Again, slower please, Miss/Sir. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Would you mind speaking slower? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You are speaking very fast. Could you slow down, please?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future tense to talk actions in the future.<br/><br/> The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is <span class=\"strong\">'ll.</span><br/><br/>You use the Future tense when you talk about intentions, make offers or make predictions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Starting Monday, I'll do educational outreach at the company. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I'll write blogs and articles for the website."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Peace Corps"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an American organization that promotes international development"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Examples: Are you joining the Peace Corps? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob10aud01"}]}, {"type"